From 52d719a04341dc51317d0ac5de444146277ba51d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xiaozhi & Tono AI Team <noreply>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:24:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(webworker-packer): keep platform rows when an overlay
 ships a home patch

The base image carries the platform rows the Worker composition requires at
home/cordis.patch.yml. An overlay that ships the same path replaces the
whole file when the host applies it, silently dropping those rows and
letting a deployment overlay change required platform config.

Give packVfsOverlay an optional platformHomePatch. When the overlay being
packed carries home/cordis.patch.yml, rewrite its patch list as the
overlay's own rows followed by the platform rows. Patch lists apply in
order with a later row replacing an earlier same-id config, so the overlay
can add or restate rows while the platform's required config still wins.
Without platformHomePatch the overlay's bytes are unchanged, and an overlay
without a home patch gains none.

Export PackOverlayOptions from the package root.

Test: packages/experimental/webworker-packer/tests/overlay-home-patch.spec.ts
packs an overlay carrying an added row and a restated platform row, then
reads the merged YAML back and asserts both lists survive with the platform
row last.
